choice LAB5_DEMO
    prompt "Lab 5 demo"
    default LAB5_DEMO_PIPELINE
    help
        Selects which of the three Lab 5 FreeRTOS demos this firmware image
        builds -- exactly one is ever compiled in (main/pipeline.c,
        main/race.c and main/inversion.c are each wrapped in
        "#if CONFIG_LAB5_DEMO_..." so only the selected file's app_main()
        exists). Switch demos with `idf.py menuconfig` (or by hand-editing
        sdkconfig) and rebuild. See the lab manual for what each one does
        and how to read its output.

    config LAB5_DEMO_PIPELINE
        bool "Sensor -> processing -> logger pipeline (queues, priorities, stack HWM)"
        help
            Three tasks glued by two queues: a 10 Hz sensor task feeds an
            8-sample moving-average processing task, which feeds a 1 Hz
            logger task. Prints "LAB5 OK avg=<t.t>" once a second and, at
            t~=30 s, each task's stack high-water mark ("LAB5 OK
            hwm_<task>=<bytes>"). This is the default, and the only demo
            exercised by qemu_smoke.sh.

    config LAB5_DEMO_RACE
        bool "Provoked race condition (unprotected counter, then mutex)"
        help
            Two equal-priority tasks each increment a shared counter 100000
            times, first with no lock at all (prints "LAB5 OK
            race_lost=<n>", n>0 -- the lost-update race), then again guarded
            by a mutex (prints "LAB5 OK race_lost=0").

    config LAB5_DEMO_INVERSION
        bool "Measured priority inversion (binary semaphore vs. mutex)"
        help
            A low-priority task takes a lock and busy-holds it; a
            medium-priority task (unrelated to the lock) hogs the CPU; a
            high-priority task blocks trying to take the same lock. Its
            blocking time is measured with esp_timer_get_time(), once with
            a plain binary semaphore ("LAB5 OK inv_sem_us=<n>") and once
            with a mutex, whose priority inheritance bounds the inversion
            ("LAB5 OK inv_mux_us=<m>"). Expect n >> m.

endchoice
